1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,520
Take me to Kirito.

2
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,880
Well, there you go.

3
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:14,157
I told you your boy was the biggest
threat to this project's security.

4
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:15,070
I know.

5
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,777
You don't have to rub it in.

6
00:00:16,860 --> 00:00:18,600
Is Kirito even safe here?

7
00:00:18,740 --> 00:00:21,177
Were you lying when you
said you could save him?

8
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:23,360
Is he alive? Answer me!

9
00:00:26,840 --> 00:00:29,580
Kanamoto injected a potent toxin into him.

10
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:34,194
It damaged Kirito's brain so much,
conventional treatment can't heal him.

11
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:41,141
But, unconventional treatment can, and the
only place with that technology is wrath.

12
00:00:41,620 --> 00:00:43,420
I'm sure he told you about it.

13
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:47,200
The STL, short for Soul Translator.

14
00:00:47,860 --> 00:00:50,900
If we use the STL to
stimulate his Fluctlight,

15
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:54,937
we can regenerate a brand new,
perfectly healthy neural network.

16
00:00:55,020 --> 00:00:56,380
But that takes time.

17
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:01,160
Right now, he's in a full-spec
STL, which can only be found here.

18
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,637
The treatment he's getting surpasses
what any hospital can offer.

19
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,900
He even has his own full-time nurse.

20
00:01:09,100 --> 00:01:09,980
Okay, then.

21
00:01:10,240 --> 00:01:11,828
I'll take your word for it.

22
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:14,680
All right, Kikwoka.

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:17,997
Since you're in the mood to talk,
might as well tell us everything.

24
00:01:18,080 --> 00:01:19,080
From the top.

25
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:23,660
First, why is an SDF official like
you using the Ministry as a front?

26
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:26,177
Next, what's the point of this?

27
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:29,100
And last, why Kirigaya specifically?

28
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,640
If you want answers,
you'll have to sign on.

29
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,407
How about you start talking?

30
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:36,997
All right, then.

31
00:01:37,080 --> 00:01:40,497
I assume you're both familiar
with the concept of the STL?

32
00:01:40,580 --> 00:01:42,320
It reads souls,

33
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:44,780
or Fluctlights as you call them,

34
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:49,431
and allows the user to dive into a
virtual world that's incredibly lifelike.

35
00:01:49,660 --> 00:01:50,490
That's correct.

36
00:01:50,573 --> 00:01:53,620
And do you know what the
objective of this project is?

37
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,260
No, I don't.

38
00:01:57,040 --> 00:02:00,960
To create a bottom-up, multi-purpose
artificial intelligence.

39
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:40,760
Let's go ahead and go ahead
and get out of the way!.

40
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:45,200
I hear a voice that I call?.

41
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:47,180
To your fingers.

42
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:53,057
I'm starting to see the end of the call.

43
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:55,780
I'm going to see the end of the call!.

44
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:59,577
Shiny song, my diamond.

45
00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:01,380
I'm going to cry and cry.

46
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:03,077
I'm going to cry?.

47
00:03:36,280 --> 00:03:39,160
A bottom-up, multi-purpose AI?

48
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:40,610
That's right.

49
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:43,317
There are two approaches
to developing an AI.

50
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:46,137
The first is called top-down
artificial intelligence,

51
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:49,497
where the AI is programmed with
experience and knowledge so that

52
00:03:49,580 --> 00:03:52,837
it learns enough to approach
something close to true intelligence.

53
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:54,357
That's pretty much the gist of it.

54
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:58,077
Everything that's an AI right now
is using that top-down approach.

55
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:58,990
Heck, Dr.

56
00:03:59,073 --> 00:04:00,857
Shige Mura was working
with us here for a bit,

57
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:03,077
and even his research focused on that.

58
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:08,260
A top-down AI, however, can't react
appropriately to things it hasn't learned about.

59
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:12,933
At this point in time, none have evolved
enough to have true intelligence.

60
00:04:14,100 --> 00:04:17,700
The second approach to AI
development is called Bottom-Up.

61
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:21,037
The human brain is an
organ comprised of 100

62
00:04:21,120 --> 00:04:23,760
billion cells connected in intricate ways.

63
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:26,757
The idea of Bottom-Up
is recreating the brain

64
00:04:26,840 --> 00:04:29,917
electronically and generating
true intelligence in it.

65
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,877
But that would be impossible to do.

66
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,200
You're right, and until now, it was.

67
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:38,140
But with the Soul Translator,
we can scan a human soul.

68
00:04:38,520 --> 00:04:42,917
Or specifically, the quantum field and
brain cells we call the Fluct Light.

69
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,637
If you're wondering where we're going
to put all the data of a human brain,

70
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,602
stop wondering.

71
00:04:47,860 --> 00:04:51,036
We made the Light Quantum
Gate Crystal, or Light Cube,

72
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,082
to store all that good stuff on.

73
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:57,417
Theoretically, you could save a
one-to-one copy of a Fluct Light.

74
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:58,382
That's correct.

75
00:04:58,780 --> 00:05:00,660
Although, it's not a theory.

76
00:05:01,440 --> 00:05:03,560
We've already copied a human soul.

77
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:08,440
But then, why did you bother
asking me to come help you?

78
00:05:08,940 --> 00:05:11,740
Because, like idiots, we missed something.

79
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,780
The human soul is complex.

80
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,780
Sure, we can copy it.

81
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,920
But there's a wide gap
between it and a true AI.

82
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:20,630
Higa?

83
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,120
Go on.

84
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:24,400
Show our guests a demonstration.

85
00:05:24,740 --> 00:05:26,480
Damn, you're sadistic.

86
00:05:32,940 --> 00:05:34,537
Is the sampling done yet?

87
00:05:34,620 --> 00:05:35,857
Yep.

88
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:36,837
No problems.

89
00:05:36,920 --> 00:05:37,837
Looking good.

90
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:39,097
Sweet.

91
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:42,377
So why is it dark and
how come I can't move?

92
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:44,117
Oh I know why.

93
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:45,057
Let me out.

94
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:46,197
The stl's glitching.

95
00:05:46,280 --> 00:05:49,277
Sorry buddy I can't log you out.

96
00:05:49,360 --> 00:05:50,737
Dude what the hell?

97
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:51,877
Let me out of here.

98
00:05:51,960 --> 00:05:53,057
Who are you?

99
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:54,657
I don't recognize your voice.

100
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:56,177
Takeru Higa.

101
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:57,560
You know that?

102
00:05:59,320 --> 00:06:00,150
What?

103
00:06:00,233 --> 00:06:01,063
No way.

104
00:06:01,146 --> 00:06:01,977
I'm Higa.

105
00:06:02,060 --> 00:06:03,557
Let me out and you'll see.

106
00:06:03,640 --> 00:06:04,470
Relax.

107
00:06:04,553 --> 00:06:07,217
You're talking to Higa the copy.

108
00:06:07,300 --> 00:06:08,437
I know.

109
00:06:08,520 --> 00:06:09,517
You know what's going on.

110
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,957
So just accept the situation. Screw you.

111
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:12,997
I'm me.

112
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:14,777
If I'm a copy then I know it.

113
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:15,690
God damn it.

114
00:06:15,773 --> 00:06:16,603
Come on.

115
00:06:16,686 --> 00:06:18,417
Please let me out.

116
00:06:18,500 --> 00:06:19,517
You son of a bitch.

117
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,957
Right now we talked about this.

118
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:23,297
You need to calm down.

119
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:27,909
If you can't think rationally your fluk
light won't be able to I am rational!

120
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:28,870
Okay, then.

121
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:31,857
Let's see who's faster
at Pi, me or that faker.

122
00:06:44,340 --> 00:06:47,280
Full collapse, one minute, eight seconds.

123
00:06:48,780 --> 00:06:50,721
Alright, that was beyond twisted.

124
00:06:50,840 --> 00:06:51,880
It is disturbing.

125
00:06:52,580 --> 00:06:57,137
Still, it's the best way to explain what
we've been able to accomplish up to now.

126
00:06:57,220 --> 00:06:58,597
I'm sorry you had to see it.

127
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:01,900
We copied over a dozen
Fluctlights, including mine,

128
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,797
and submitted them to the same test.

129
00:07:03,880 --> 00:07:05,617
The results were always the same.

130
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:08,759
Their logic systems went
haywire and they collapsed.

131
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:12,397
Since mature Fluctlights don't
work, what would you try next?

132
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:14,009
Maybe wipe their memories?

133
00:07:14,520 --> 00:07:16,720
Or raise a soul from scratch.

134
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:18,280
You didn't.

135
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:19,540
Yes, we did.

136
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:23,600
We put newborns into the
STL and copied their souls.

137
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:28,077
These copies are essentially
human, so how would you raise them?

138
00:07:28,160 --> 00:07:29,017
Not in a void.

139
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:31,629
You'd need an exact
copy of the real world.

140
00:07:31,740 --> 00:07:32,637
That's impossible.

141
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:34,280
We can't do that yet.

142
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:38,600
So, we went looking for an
alternative, and we found it online.

143
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:41,000
VRMMO Worlds.

144
00:07:41,760 --> 00:07:43,060
Tonkii, you're sharp.

145
00:07:43,660 --> 00:07:47,357
Using the seed, we made our own
world, with villages and terrain,

146
00:07:47,440 --> 00:07:50,600
and converted it to mnemonic
visuals for the STL.

147
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:54,017
We placed four of our staff in
the first village we created.

148
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:56,860
They acted as parents to 16 AI infants,

149
00:07:57,140 --> 00:08:00,316
or soul architects, and
raised them till they were 18.

150
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:04,397
We monitored the
youngsters as they grew up.

151
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:08,127
Oh, by the way, officially we
call them artificial Fluctlights.

152
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:12,077
Anyway, we were more than
satisfied with how they turned out.

153
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:14,700
They were sharp, obedient, and upstanding.

154
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:17,357
When they eventually paired up,

155
00:08:17,440 --> 00:08:21,205
we made them parents and gave
them new soul archetypes to raise.

156
00:08:21,560 --> 00:08:23,037
Our staff was out by then,

157
00:08:23,120 --> 00:08:27,600
so we accelerated time by 5,000 and
soon we had multiple generations.

158
00:08:28,340 --> 00:08:32,680
After three weeks had passed in our
world, 300 had passed in theirs.

159
00:08:33,040 --> 00:08:37,540
Now, they have a fully functioning
society with a population of 80,000.

160
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,800
You simulated an entire civilization.

161
00:08:41,560 --> 00:08:42,390
Exactly.

162
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:45,340
So far, 480 years have passed there.

163
00:08:45,640 --> 00:08:49,340
The capital, Senator, has
20,000 citizens living in it.

164
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:50,520
At this point,

165
00:08:50,660 --> 00:08:55,366
all the AI Fluctlights have matured into
the bottom-up AIs we were shooting for.

166
00:08:55,520 --> 00:08:58,497
We were all ready to hit the next
phase and were stoked about it.

167
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,577
But then...

168
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:03,140
We noticed a major issue,
which stood in our way.

169
00:09:03,860 --> 00:09:04,740
What issue?

170
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:07,477
The governing body there
called the Axiom Church

171
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:10,360
created a set of laws
called the Taboo Index.

172
00:09:10,740 --> 00:09:11,820
The what index?

173
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,460
The Taboo Index.

174
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:17,546
It contains laws like one forbidding
murder, just like we have.

175
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,957
And, if you've been
watching the news recently,

176
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:22,617
you can see how difficult that
one is for humans to obey.

177
00:09:22,700 --> 00:09:25,857
But the Fluctlights obey all
their laws to the letter.

178
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,640
They're obsessive about it.

179
00:09:28,780 --> 00:09:31,520
This town is beautiful, but too perfect.

180
00:09:32,060 --> 00:09:35,472
There's no litter on the streets
and no crime to speak of.

181
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:39,517
Needless to say, there's not been a
single murder committed here either.

182
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:42,188
And that would be a
good thing, wouldn't it?

183
00:09:43,240 --> 00:09:44,260
It wouldn't.

184
00:09:44,460 --> 00:09:45,636
Not for him, anyway.

185
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:48,980
He wants AIs that can kill.

186
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:52,117
Kirito and I were wrong.

187
00:09:52,200 --> 00:09:55,500
We thought we knew why you
were interested in VR Miss.

188
00:09:55,620 --> 00:09:56,460
For training.

189
00:09:56,740 --> 00:10:00,564
We figured you'd use the technology
to train soldiers and police.

190
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:05,560
But for an officer of the SDF to
attempt something on this scale,

191
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:07,545
there has to be more at stake.

192
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:09,480
And there is.

193
00:10:09,700 --> 00:10:12,460
This project is about
creating AI for warfare.

194
00:10:13,140 --> 00:10:13,970
Isn't it?

195
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:17,900
Is that true, Kikwoka?

196
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:25,100
Five years ago, when the NerveGear
was first announced, I had an idea.

197
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:27,797
Although it was meant for gaming,

198
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:31,939
this new technology had the potential
to change how wars were fought.

199
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,840
When the SAO incident happened,

200
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:39,651
I asked to be transferred to the Ministry,
then joined the task force there.

201
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:43,254
That was all so I could get
this project off the ground.

202
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,900
And five years later, here we are.

203
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:51,597
That's his reason but why did
you decide to take part in this?

204
00:10:51,680 --> 00:10:54,720
Oh, um, that's a whole
nother story for me.

205
00:10:54,820 --> 00:10:55,650
It's personal

206
00:10:56,200 --> 00:10:57,337
When I was in college,

207
00:10:57,420 --> 00:10:59,497
I had a bud in Korea who was in the army

208
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:02,168
there and he got killed
on one of his tours.

209
00:11:02,780 --> 00:11:07,437
So I thought this stupid world ain't
gonna stop having wars anytime soon!

210
00:11:07,520 --> 00:11:11,800
But if we could figure out how to
have them without killing people then?

211
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:13,996
Sounds naive, right?

212
00:11:14,740 --> 00:11:18,800
You didn't tell Kirito any of this
before you hired him, did you?

213
00:11:19,140 --> 00:11:20,680
Would it matter if I did?

214
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:22,460
Yes, it would have.

215
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:25,617
If you had told him, he never
would have agreed to help.

216
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:29,171
There's one important issue
your plan doesn't even address.

217
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,360
Which is?

218
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:33,080
The rights of the AIs.

219
00:11:33,820 --> 00:11:36,700
These things you call
artificial flufflights?

220
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:39,557
They're still mentally
and emotionally human.

221
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:42,581
True, but it's not like
they have physical bodies.

222
00:11:42,760 --> 00:11:44,897
But otherwise, they're
no different from us,

223
00:11:44,980 --> 00:11:47,880
and you're forcing them
to be your tools of war.

224
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,720
Kirito would never agree to that. Ever.

225
00:11:52,280 --> 00:11:55,337
Look, I understand the point
you're trying to make here,

226
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:56,920
but to me,

227
00:11:57,080 --> 00:12:01,680
the life of one SDF soldier is worth
far more than a hundred thousand AIs.

228
00:12:05,720 --> 00:12:08,440
Anyway, why did you
need Kirigaya for this?

229
00:12:08,980 --> 00:12:13,686
I can't understand why you'd use a civilian
on a project that's so confidential.

230
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:14,740
I'm sorry.

231
00:12:15,020 --> 00:12:18,844
I got so carried away talking
about the project, I almost forgot.

232
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:23,580
We needed to know why the AI Fluctlights
couldn't disobey the Taboo Index.

233
00:12:24,020 --> 00:12:26,360
So, I came up with an experiment.

234
00:12:27,520 --> 00:12:30,937
If we blocked a human's memories,
reverted him to childhood,

235
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:33,320
and had him grow up in our VR world,

236
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:36,560
would he be able to
disobey the Taboo Index?

237
00:12:37,560 --> 00:12:42,501
To carry this out, we needed someone with
experience navigating in a VR environment.

238
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:45,397
Not just a week or a
month's worth of experience.

239
00:12:45,480 --> 00:12:46,620
I'm talking years.

240
00:12:49,500 --> 00:12:50,920
That's why I needed him.

241
00:12:53,440 --> 00:12:57,028
I can't believe Kazuto would
sign up for something like that.

242
00:12:58,420 --> 00:13:01,560
Can we even trust anything
Kikuoka says anymore?

243
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:05,369
I bet he only told you a fraction
of what he's really up to.

244
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:10,345
I guess all we can do now is hope the
treatment Kirito gets in the STL will work.

245
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:13,771
What happened with that taboo index thing?

246
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:15,571
You know, the experiment.

247
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,546
Did he tell you if it worked?

248
00:13:18,640 --> 00:13:22,464
Kirito got to be close friends
with two others, a boy and a girl.

249
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:26,134
Kikuoka said the girl ended
up breaking one of the laws.

250
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:27,130
Really?

251
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:30,100
Did she do it because of Kirito? Uh-huh.

252
00:13:30,920 --> 00:13:35,440
Apparently she violated a taboo by
trying to access a restricted address.

253
00:13:36,900 --> 00:13:41,841
According to the log, the girl saw another
AI Fluctlight die in the restricted area.

254
00:13:42,020 --> 00:13:45,220
From what we can tell, she
was trying to save him.

255
00:13:45,460 --> 00:13:48,137
She had more concern for
another person's life

256
00:13:48,220 --> 00:13:50,808
than she had for
disobeying the taboo index.

257
00:13:51,020 --> 00:13:54,196
She chose to do it, and
that's what we're looking for.

258
00:13:57,020 --> 00:13:58,667
That's kind of a neat story.

259
00:13:59,540 --> 00:14:02,952
Yeah, if only it wasn't about
training AIs to kill people.

260
00:14:03,660 --> 00:14:04,490
You're right.

261
00:14:04,573 --> 00:14:06,500
But look at what she did.

262
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:10,120
She went against the system
just to help someone else.

263
00:14:10,480 --> 00:14:13,160
Does this AI girl have a name? Yes.

264
00:14:16,140 --> 00:14:17,940
Alice? That's right.

265
00:14:18,240 --> 00:14:20,064
I was stunned when I found out.

266
00:14:20,620 --> 00:14:23,057
Her having that name is
quite the coincidence.

267
00:14:23,140 --> 00:14:25,440
The name ALICE, you see,

268
00:14:25,700 --> 00:14:27,997
also happens to be the
name of the concept that

269
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:31,780
was the foundation for Wrath
and this project. Concept?

270
00:14:32,960 --> 00:14:36,237
An AI that is highly
adaptive and autonomous.

271
00:14:36,320 --> 00:14:37,460
More specifically,

272
00:14:37,880 --> 00:14:43,840
an artificial labile intelligent
cybernated existence, or the acronym ALICE.

273
00:14:45,200 --> 00:14:49,560
Our goal, ultimately, was to turn
an AI Fluctlight into an ALICE.

274
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:56,160
Therefore, we called
it Project Alicization.

275
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:59,757
That sounds so complicated!

276
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:02,777
Yeah, I don't understand a
lot of what he said either.

277
00:15:02,860 --> 00:15:06,117
But he said if they had
saved Alice's floodlight?

278
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:08,837
Their research would be
much further along by now.

279
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:10,620
Did she die?

280
00:15:11,120 --> 00:15:15,540
No, she's still alive But remember I
said time there's faster than here?

281
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:16,670
Mm-hmm

282
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:20,700
Well, by the time they noticed,
two days had gone by there.

283
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:25,508
She was taken to the capital, and the
Axiom Church had her Fluctlight altered.

284
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:27,060
They changed her soul?

285
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:31,653
How could they give AI Fluctlights
that kind of authority over each other?

286
00:15:31,920 --> 00:15:36,757
They don't really know how it happened, but
they think it might be a system exploit.

287
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:40,546
A few of the AI Fluctlights can
use what they call sacred arts.

288
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:44,935
They're basically system access
authorities that look like magic spells.

289
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:48,197
Sorry I have to log out now?

290
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,110
Why?

291
00:15:49,193 --> 00:15:50,023
What's the rush?

292
00:15:50,106 --> 00:15:53,097
They said they'd let me
look in on Kirito for a bit.

293
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:54,857
I don't want to be late for that.

294
00:15:54,940 --> 00:15:56,697
You get to watch him sleep.

295
00:15:56,780 --> 00:15:57,857
Tell us if he drools.

296
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:59,777
I don't.

297
00:15:59,860 --> 00:16:01,097
I don't think I'll see his face.

298
00:16:01,180 --> 00:16:03,121
The machine he sent covers it up.

299
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:16,820
Number four, and that's five.

300
00:16:17,420 --> 00:16:19,185
They're still building Unit 6.

301
00:16:19,400 --> 00:16:22,060
It's in Roppongi with
Unit 1, the prototype.

302
00:16:23,140 --> 00:16:24,457
Two and three are here.

303
00:16:24,540 --> 00:16:27,069
Well, actually, they're
in the lower shaft.

304
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:28,170
Ms. Aki.

305
00:16:29,180 --> 00:16:30,720
What are you doing here?

306
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:32,900
I'm taking care of Kirigaya.

307
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:36,420
But you were his nurse at
that hospital in Chiyoda.

308
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:39,987
Wait, are you a nurse
or are you just faking?

309
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:41,920
I'm a nurse.

310
00:16:42,100 --> 00:16:45,197
I'm registered and everything
and have the papers to prove it.

311
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:47,020
Although, full disclosure,

312
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:52,441
the nursing school I graduated from is
affiliated with the Tokyo Self-Defense Force.

313
00:16:53,280 --> 00:16:55,177
Sergeant First Class Natsuki Aki.

314
00:16:55,260 --> 00:17:00,200
As long as I'm on duty here, I swear
I will protect Kitty Gaia. We good?

315
00:17:03,620 --> 00:17:05,020
Yeah, we're good.

316
00:17:05,320 --> 00:17:07,085
Don't you worry about a thing.

317
00:17:11,620 --> 00:17:14,580
In your opinion, will he be okay?

318
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:16,780
Of course he will.

319
00:17:16,980 --> 00:17:20,497
His Fluctlight's stable so far, and
his neural network's on the mend.

320
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,597
All his vitals are looking good, too.

321
00:17:22,680 --> 00:17:23,937
He is a tough cookie.

322
00:17:24,020 --> 00:17:26,560
He's the one who cleared SAO, after all.

323
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:38,160
Can we talk?

324
00:17:41,660 --> 00:17:44,740
There's something I
have to confess to you.

325
00:17:46,620 --> 00:17:47,940
Not just to you.

326
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:52,920
I owe one to all the SAO
players, living and dead.

327
00:17:54,320 --> 00:17:58,200
I'm sure you heard the story
about how during the SAO incident,

328
00:17:58,400 --> 00:18:01,929
Akihiko Kayaba and I were hiding
in the mountains of Nagano.

329
00:18:04,380 --> 00:18:07,840
That scars from a micro-bomb
Akihiko implanted there.

330
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:12,037
The news said he put it
there to force me to stay

331
00:18:12,120 --> 00:18:15,061
and help him with his plan
during those two years.

332
00:18:15,320 --> 00:18:16,791
But that's not the truth.

333
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:21,440
Yes, the bomb was real, but
I knew it would never go off.

334
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:24,417
He put it there so that
when we were caught,

335
00:18:24,500 --> 00:18:27,265
I wouldn't be charged
with aiding and abetting.

336
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:32,460
It was a bluff to keep me safe, and
the only present he ever gave me.

337
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:37,077
When Akihiko got into the
Toto Institute of Technology,

338
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:39,748
he was already head of
development at Argus.

339
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:42,106
But I didn't know about that.

340
00:18:42,700 --> 00:18:46,465
All I saw was a scrawny loner who
only cared about his research.

341
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,100
You want some inspiration?

342
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,540
Then get out once in a while.

343
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:02,840
I need to find a way to emulate the
feeling of sunlight on the skin.

344
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:04,350
What?

345
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:08,280
We were total opposites,
but we started dating.

346
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:15,700
One thing I could never figure out
was why he wanted to stay with me.

347
00:19:17,780 --> 00:19:19,280
The other was him.

348
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:22,780
all that time together.

349
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:27,780
And I didn't know him at all.

350
00:19:29,120 --> 00:19:34,380
I knew Akihiko was at his cabin, but I
didn't go there because I wanted to help him.

351
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,070
I...

352
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:40,640
I went because I wanted to kill him.

353
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:47,117
And then, I don't know why, but I...

354
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,180
I...

355
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,220
I couldn't do it.

356
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,940
He knew what I was thinking,
and that I had a knife.

357
00:19:56,280 --> 00:20:00,200
But he just smiled and said,
What am I going to do with you?

358
00:20:00,440 --> 00:20:01,720
Like he always did.

359
00:20:02,140 --> 00:20:04,120
And then he went back to Aincrad.

360
00:20:08,900 --> 00:20:11,120
Oh God, I'm so sorry.

361
00:20:14,940 --> 00:20:18,440
Kirito and I never blamed you
or hated you for anything.

362
00:20:19,220 --> 00:20:20,597
To tell you the truth.

363
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:23,637
I can't really say I hate
the commander either.

364
00:20:23,720 --> 00:20:26,420
I mean, Akihiko Kayaba.

365
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:35,677
I'm not saying he should be
forgiven for what he did.

366
00:20:35,760 --> 00:20:36,937
He shouldn't.

367
00:20:37,020 --> 00:20:39,120
A lot of lives were lost.

368
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:43,600
But still, and this may
sound a little selfish.

369
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:48,847
I wouldn't trade anything for the time
I got to spend living there with Kirito.

370
00:20:50,080 --> 00:20:53,720
Honestly, to me, those were
the best days of my life.

371
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,417
Yes, the commander committed a crime.

372
00:20:58,500 --> 00:21:00,157
And so did Kirito and I.

373
00:21:00,240 --> 00:21:01,777
And you did too.

374
00:21:01,860 --> 00:21:03,577
We all did something wrong.

375
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:07,895
But in the end, even if we're punished,
there's no way to make it right.

376
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:11,893
I don't think the day will
ever come when we're forgiven.

377
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:14,360
All we can do is own up to it.

378
00:21:14,600 --> 00:21:17,776
There's no choice but to
face our sins and keep going.

379
00:21:28,420 --> 00:21:30,120
Coming all the way out here?

380
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:32,487
What am I gonna do with you?

381
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:37,617
It's so early.

382
00:21:37,700 --> 00:21:39,820
Come back to bed.

383
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:56,217
Was that?

384
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:58,380
A dream?

385
00:22:09,740 --> 00:22:16,740
go.

386
00:22:39,380 --> 00:22:41,960
So you are just smiling.

387
00:22:43,080 --> 00:22:44,657
I want to see you when I am.

388
00:22:44,740 --> 00:22:46,797
I want you to protect me.

389
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:51,157
I want you to feel

390
00:22:54,300 --> 00:22:57,437
I've received my eyes.

391
00:22:57,520 --> 00:23:02,177
I've always seen my eyes on my face.

392
00:23:02,260 --> 00:23:04,084
I've been able to hold my eyes.

393
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:09,277
It's not a picture of your back.

394
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:12,637
Game no so no nabushii sa wo.

395
00:23:12,720 --> 00:23:17,217
Iska to Nori de kanji ra Rider.

396
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:19,277
Kaku Sheyta ita.

397
00:23:19,360 --> 00:23:21,397
So no kizu wo.

398
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:26,457
Sukoshi ne mo i yasetatara ii na.

399
00:23:26,540 --> 00:23:30,160
Realistu yuuu.

400
00:23:40,340 --> 00:23:41,780
Thank you.
